92186179885 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179885 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179885 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179885 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179885 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Exponential Equations With Different Bases Using Logarithms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179885 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186180588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179885 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179885 #edb/ref 1050 960.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179885 #edb/ref 1050 960.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186179885 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2bda390c-2c58-5a3b-8f52-4a654f72417d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180141 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186178420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180141 #edb/ref 1069 "q-233243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180141 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180141 #edb/ref 1071 "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${e}^{3x+1}={2}^{x-1}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180141 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3a4d2c64-ecf2-540e-86cd-1d47fbb20b4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180141 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3x+1} & ={2}^{x-1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3x+1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{x-1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{x-1}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+1 & =(x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+1 & =(x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 3x+1 & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 3x-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-1 \\\\ x(3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)) & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1}{3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180588 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180588 #edb/ref 1061 458851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180588 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eb38f75d-c8b6-5802-b9e9-b651b8926880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180588 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180589 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180589 #edb/ref 1061 458852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180589 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4eb5d9eb-6736-57e9-b46f-2d5f8256c8a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180589 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180590 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180590 #edb/ref 1061 458855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180590 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "de4820e0-a2d9-5e96-a747-0c2e47ba3d63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180590 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180591 #edb/ref 1061 458858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180591 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "abcd0701-4558-5a9c-88e2-021815594bde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180591 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180666 #edb/ref 1064 "The most general way of solving exponential equations with different bases is to use logarithms on both sides of the equation. \nFor example, given the equation\n\n$$\n3^{x+1} = 5^{x},\n$$\n\nwe could apply $\\log_3$ on both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\log_3(3^{x+1}) = \\log_3(5^{x}).\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b \\left( b^c \\right) = c$ to simplify the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & ={log}_{3}⁡({5}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law for logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =x{log}_{3}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =x{log}_{3}⁡(5) \\\\ x-x{log}_{3}⁡(5) & =-1 \\\\ x(1-{log}_{3}⁡(5)) & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{1-{log}_{3}⁡(5)} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{{log}_{3}⁡(5)-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** in the first step, we also could have applied $\\log_5$ on both sides of our equation, instead of $\\log_3.$ Then, the answer would be numerically the same but expressed using $\\log_5$ instead of $\\log_3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180666 #edb/ref 1065 2799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180666 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "46223175-9314-5060-b3a3-dc01af9f1b38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180666 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236191 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236191 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236191 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3bbf73f4-86d1-5bfd-9e9d-5a3cfdc63e3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236198 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236198 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236198 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3cac3a9a-26b3-5ebf-89d6-f1f0bfe75ca1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236332 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236332 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236332 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "50640e0e-0e74-5967-8122-cf3f2c127102" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236469 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236469 #e